From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:15:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 88W8964: check the skb_copy() of (re)association
 responses

pcie_tx_xmit_ndp() reports the status of (re)association responses
from a copy, but used the copy without checking that skb_copy()
succeeded. Skip the early report when the copy fails.

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
[Robert Peerenboom: split out of neheb/mwlwifi (upstream branch) commit
 92b4dd1 ("88W8964: return all TX frames to mac80211 and fix TX path
 bugs") and backported to db97edf2 on top of the OpenWrt patches]
Signed-off-by: Robert Peerenboom <development@mindrush.de>
---
 hif/pcie/8964/tx_ndp.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/hif/pcie/8964/tx_ndp.c
+++ b/hif/pcie/8964/tx_ndp.c
@@ -601,9 +601,11 @@ void pcie_tx_xmit_ndp(struct ieee80211_h
 			struct ieee80211_tx_info *ack_info;
 
 			ack_skb = skb_copy(skb, GFP_ATOMIC);
-			ack_info = IEEE80211_SKB_CB(ack_skb);
-			pcie_tx_prepare_info(priv, 0, ack_info);
-			ieee80211_tx_status_skb(hw, ack_skb);
+			if (ack_skb) {
+				ack_info = IEEE80211_SKB_CB(ack_skb);
+				pcie_tx_prepare_info(priv, 0, ack_info);
+				ieee80211_tx_status_skb(hw, ack_skb);
+			}
 		}
 
 		pcie_tx_encapsulate_frame(priv, skb, k_conf);
